#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:13
msgid "Usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:42
msgid "If you put more stuff in it, then items will fall out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:44
msgid ""
"If you try to put an oversized thing in it, then it'll fall out right "
"away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:47
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:49
msgid ""
"`max` The maximum size of the cache, checked by applying the length "
"function to all values in the cache.  Not setting this is kind of silly, "
"since that's the whole purpose of this lib, but it defaults to "
"`Infinity`.  Setting it to a non-number or negative number will throw a "
"`TypeError`.  Setting it to 0 makes it be `Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:54
msgid ""
"`maxAge` Maximum age in ms.  Items are not pro-actively pruned out as "
"they age, but if you try to get an item that is too old, it'll drop it "
"and return undefined instead of giving it to you. Setting this to a "
"negative value will make everything seem old! Setting it to a non-number "
"will throw a `TypeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`length` Function that is used to calculate the length of stored items.  "
"If you're storing strings or buffers, then you probably want to do "
"something like `function(n, key){return n.length}`.  The default is "
"`function(){return 1}`, which is fine if you want to store `max` like-"
"sized things.  The item is passed as the first argument, and the key is "
"passed as the second argumnet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:65
msgid ""
"`dispose` Function that is called on items when they are dropped from the"
" cache.  This can be handy if you want to close file descriptors or do "
"other cleanup tasks when items are no longer accessible.  Called with "
"`key, value`.  It's called *before* actually removing the item from the "
"internal cache, so if you want to immediately put it back in, you'll have"
" to do that in a `nextTick` or `setTimeout` callback or it won't do "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:72
msgid ""
"`stale` By default, if you set a `maxAge`, it'll only actually pull stale"
" items out of the cache when you `get(key)`.  (That is, it's not pre-"
"emptively doing a `setTimeout` or anything.)  If you set `stale:true`, "
"it'll return the stale value before deleting it.  If you don't set this, "
"then it'll return `undefined` when you try to get a stale entry, as if it"
" had already been deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:78
msgid ""
"`noDisposeOnSet` By default, if you set a `dispose()` method, then it'll "
"be called whenever a `set()` operation overwrites an existing key.  If "
"you set this option, `dispose()` will only be called when a key falls out"
" of the cache, not when it is overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:82
msgid ""
"`updateAgeOnGet` When using time-expiring entries with `maxAge`, setting "
"this to `true` will make each item's effective time update to the current"
" time whenever it is retrieved from cache, causing it to not expire.  (It"
" can still fall out of cache based on recency of use, of course.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:88
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:90
msgid "`set(key, value, maxAge)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:91
msgid "`get(key) => value`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:93
msgid ""
"Both of these will update the \"recently used\"-ness of the key.   They "
"do what you think. `maxAge` is optional and overrides the   cache "
"`maxAge` option if provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:97
msgid "If the key is not found, `get()` will return `undefined`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:99
msgid "The key and val can be any value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:101
msgid "`peek(key)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:103
msgid ""
"Returns the key value (or `undefined` if not found) without   updating "
"the \"recently used\"-ness of the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:106
msgid ""
"(If you find yourself using this a lot, you *might* be using the   wrong "
"sort of data structure, but there are some use cases where   it's handy.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:110
msgid "`del(key)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:112
msgid "Deletes a key out of the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:114
msgid "`reset()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:116
msgid "Clear the cache entirely, throwing away all values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:118
msgid "`has(key)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:120
msgid ""
"Check if a key is in the cache, without updating the recent-ness   or "
"deleting it for being stale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:123
msgid "`forEach(function(value,key,cache), [thisp])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:125
msgid ""
"Just like `Array.prototype.forEach`.  Iterates over all the keys   in the"
" cache, in order of recent-ness.  (Ie, more recently used   items are "
"iterated over first.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:129
msgid "`rforEach(function(value,key,cache), [thisp])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:131
msgid ""
"The same as `cache.forEach(...)` but items are iterated over in   reverse"
" order.  (ie, less recently used items are iterated over   first.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:135
msgid "`keys()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:137
msgid "Return an array of the keys in the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:139
msgid "`values()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:141
msgid "Return an array of the values in the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:143
msgid "`length`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:145
msgid ""
"Return total length of objects in cache taking into account   `length` "
"options function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:148
msgid "`itemCount`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:150
msgid ""
"Return total quantity of objects currently in cache. Note, that   `stale`"
" (see options) items are returned as part of this item   count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:154
msgid "`dump()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:156
msgid ""
"Return an array of the cache entries ready for serialization and usage   "
"with 'destinationCache.load(arr)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:159
msgid "`load(cacheEntriesArray)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:161
msgid ""
"Loads another cache entries array, obtained with `sourceCache.dump()`,   "
"into the cache. The destination cache is reset before loading new entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:164
msgid "`prune()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/lru-cache_README.md:166
msgid "Manually iterates over the entire cache proactively pruning old entries"
msgstr ""

